<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

''INFER — The excerpt does not identify the fault or justify a specific fix yet.'' It proves the client accepted a verified gate verdict, but it does not show whether B received A’s Automerge join, replied with its peer ID, or whether A later disconnected. The earlier `findWhenReady` fault occurs after this assertion and is a separate observation problem.

''MEASURED —'' The failing run logged “verdict OK — crossing open, syncing” before timing out; the test took about 6.2 seconds. That log precedes `join()`, not receipt of B’s Automerge peer message. [[Failure excerpt|/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/controller/terra-dial-fault/fail-excerpt.log:19]], [[client adapter|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/lar-ws-client-adapter.ts:330]].

''MEASURED — Possible paths to no matching peer:''

* Before that log, an absent or unreadable pin, invalid presentation, gate refusal, deadline, transport failure, or named chain answer prevents a successful crossing. Silence triggers redial; named answers and local refusals anergize. These paths do not explain the logged successful crossing itself. [[Dial|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/lar-ws-client-adapter.ts:302]], [[gate|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-gate.ts:620]].
* After the verdict, session opening or the channel can fail; the join or response can be lost, malformed, rejected for protocol incompatibility, or delayed. B’s adapter emits a response containing ''its adapter’s'' peer ID after receiving a valid join; A emits `peer-candidate` from the response’s `senderId`, which the subsystem forwards as `peer`. Thus a different sender ID also fails the exact comparison. [[Gate seat|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-gate.ts:541]], [[server adapter|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/node_modules/@automerge/automerge-repo-network-websocket/dist/WebSocketServerAdapter.js:146]], [[client adapter|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/node_modules/@automerge/automerge-repo-network-websocket/dist/WebSocketClientAdapter.js:160]].
* ''INFER —'' A server adapter that has not installed its `connection` listener when the gate opens could miss the socket. The rig returns after constructing the Repo, while adapter connection is scheduled through a metadata promise; this timing needs a controlled witness, not an assumption that it occurred in CI. [[Rig|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/tests/gated-node-rig.ts:53]], [[subsystem|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/node_modules/@automerge/automerge-repo/dist/network/NetworkSubsystem.js:75]].

''MEASURED —'' An early `peer` event alone is not missed: the helper subscribes and immediately checks `repo.peers`; the Repo adds the peer synchronously in its earlier listener. An early peer followed by disconnection //can// be missed because removal erases that current state. [[Test|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/tests/nexus-client-dial.test.ts:94]], [[Repo|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/node_modules/@automerge/automerge-repo/dist/Repo.js:137]].

''MEASURED —'' PR #171 makes persona admission verify the per-face ward key and `wardPop`; ward acts judge co-signs and readers validate the spend at its cited frontier. This test’s presenter instead uses the fixture’s synthetic Nexus carriage admit, not that persona admission or ward-act path. A gate can still refuse its presented admit, but the verified verdict excludes such refusal for the logged crossing. [[Persona fold|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/persona-act.ts:113]], [[frozen spend|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/ward-cosign.ts:134]], [[fixture|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/tests/face-gate-fixture.ts:330]].

''INFER —'' The 6-second timeout bounds a real asynchronous join, but also masks a permanently lost message, wrong ID, or disconnected peer; increasing it cannot distinguish them. The separate dial deadline is two seconds and already passed for the logged verified crossing. [[Test|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/tests/nexus-client-dial.test.ts:153]], [[deadline|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/tests/flow-floor-rig.ts:42]].

''INFER — Minimal next red and cure:'' First add a deterministic, no-load witness that controls server-listener installation versus gate open and records join, response ID, client `peer-candidate`, subsystem `peer`, and disconnect. It must fail for the demonstrated ordering, with a control that reaches the expected peer; preserve equivalent diagnostics in the live test. If it proves the listener race, fix server readiness at the actual listener-installed event before accepting crossings. If it instead proves a transient peer, register the test’s `peer` observer before mounting and retain the event, while separately asserting connection when needed. Do not choose either cure before the red identifies the path.

''MEASURED —'' No files were written or tests run. Socket tests are ''lead runs''; the inspected installed Automerge code is local evidence and its exact CI artifact was not verified.

